# Line endings.
#
# This repository is edited on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) and run on Linux.
# A shell script checked out with CRLF has "#!/usr/bin/env bash\r" as its first
# line, and the kernel then looks for an interpreter literally called "bash\r".
# The error is "command not found", which sends you looking for a missing
# package rather than a line ending.
#
# Normalise text in the repository, and pin LF for everything Linux executes.
* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF: PowerShell is fine either way, but a .bat
# with LF endings can misbehave.
*.ps1       text eol=crlf
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries.
*.wpress    binary
*.zip       binary
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.woff2     binary
*.pdf       binary
